# Agent surface

This is where NIL spends its boldness. Everything else in the app is quiet chrome; the
stream is the one place craft is visible. Reference point: the way a modern agent client
shows its work — a tool call is a first-class, inspectable object, not a log line.

## The tool card

Every tool invocation renders as a card with four zones, in this order:

1. **Header** — tool name in `--font-ui`, primary argument in `--font-machine`
   (`nmap · 10.0.4.0/24`). Header alone is enough to understand what happened.
2. **State** — `pending` → `running` → `ok | error`. `running` drives SCANLINE on the
   card edge. State is never communicated by color alone; it carries a glyph and a label.
3. **Result** — collapsed by default, expands via REVEAL to intrinsic height. Long output
   gets its own scroll container with a scroll affordance, never an unbounded page.
4. **Gutter** — index and TRACE spine segment connecting to the next step.

Rules: never hide a failed call behind a collapsed card — errors expand by default and
state the exit code and stderr head. Never truncate output silently; show a byte count
and a "Show all" affordance. Never render a tool result as prose the agent wrote about
it — show the actual output.

## Streaming

Text streams token-by-token with the caret visible. Values the machine resolved
(hostnames, IPs, CVEs, hashes, CVSS) arrive via SCRAMBLE and settle. The stream
autoscrolls **only while pinned to the bottom**; the moment the user scrolls up, pinning
releases and a "Jump to latest" affordance appears. Silently yanking a reading user back
to the bottom is the single worst bug this surface can ship.

Interruptibility is a feature: a visible Stop control at all times during a run, and
stopping leaves the partial stream intact and labeled as interrupted.

## Findings inspector

A finding is evidence-first. Order: severity chip and CVSS vector, the observed evidence
(machine font, verbatim), then the assessment and remediation (UI font, NIL's voice).
Never lead with prose. Never show a severity without the vector that produced it — an
unsourced score is not a finding.

Severity uses the `--sev-*` ramp plus a shape/label, so it survives greyscale printing
and color-vision differences. Confidence and severity are separate fields and are never
collapsed into one number.

## Density and restraint

The stream is long and read for hours. No per-step entrance animation beyond opacity, no
hover lift on stream rows (only on the interactive controls inside them), no decorative
icons. TRACE plus the gutter index is the only structural ornament, and it is load-bearing.
